== Food Preference Effect ==

This effect triggers when a trainer feeds a food item to a monster. Each monster has two taste attributes:
* '''Warm Taste''': Their preferred flavor type.
* '''Cold Taste''': Their secondary flavor aversion or affinity.

When food is given with specific taste tags, the effect compares those tags to the monster’s tastes and adjusts the bond between them accordingly.

=== Taste Matching ===
The comparison yields one of five outcomes:

{| class="wikitable"
! Taste Alignment !! Result !! Bond Change
|-
| Both warm and cold taste tags match the monster || '''Great''' || +10
|-
| One taste matches || '''Good''' || +5
|-
| Both tags are the opposite of monster’s preferences || '''Terrible''' || -10
|-
| One tag is the opposite || '''Bad''' || -5
|-
| Neither match nor oppose || '''Average''' || 0
|}

Opposite taste relationships are defined by the effect and can be viewed on [[Taste Food]].

Feeding the right dish creates a strong emotional bond. Feeding the wrong dish… not so much.